From: Enceka <enceka@yeah.net>
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: record trusted QDMA PON unbound events

Keep a single consumable descriptor event in each software PON candidate.
Record the actual Bank0 row separately from the unbound software hash, with
the candidate serial, flow generation, original identity and GEM service.
Only the PON WAN-QDMA UNB_RATE path publishes events; ER observation and
ordinary host learning retain their existing behavior. Recheck candidates
under flow_offload_mutex and ppe_lock when consuming an event, and clear
events on conflict, withdrawal and Bank0 retirement. No worker or hardware
operation is introduced.

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.h
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.h
@@ -567,6 +567,11 @@
 	u8 band, bss;
 };
 
+struct airoha_pon_unbound_event {
+	u64 serial, generation;
+	u32 hardware_hash, service, key[19];
+};
